<% set_meta_tags title: "Privacy Policy",
                 description: "How ArogyaM collects, uses, protects, and gives you control over your personal information." %>

<%= render "shared/page_header",
           eyebrow: "Your information",
           title: "Privacy policy",
           description: "How ArogyaM collects, uses, and protects the information you share with us." %>

<div class="container page-section">
<div class="privacy-policy">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

  <div class="mb-3"><strong>Last updated: August 19, 2026</strong></div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    This Privacy Policy ("Policy") explains how ArogyaM ("we," "us," "our") collects, uses, and shares the personal information of users ("you") who sign up for our services through our user sign-up form. Please read this Policy carefully to understand our practices regarding your personal information.
  </div>

  <h3>1. Information We Collect</h3>

  <div>
    When you sign up for our services using our user sign-up form, we may collect the following types of information:
  </div>

  <ul>
    <li>
      (a) Personal Information: We collect personal information that you voluntarily provide to us, such as your name, email address, phone number, and mailing address, date of birth, gender,  and health information.
    </li>
    <li>
      (b) Device and Usage Information: We may automatically collect information about your device and how you use our services, such as your IP address, browser type, operating system, and the date and time of your visit.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2. How We Use Your Information</h3>

  <div>
    We use your personal information for the following purposes:
  </div>

  <ul>
    <li>
      (a) To provide our services to you, including making sure you are a good fit for our health programmes, creating and managing your account, responding to your inquiries, and sending you relevant communications.
    </li>
    <li>
      (b) To improve our services, such as by analyzing user behavior, conducting research, and developing new features and functionalities.
    </li>
    <li>
      (c) To send you marketing communications, including newsletters, promotions, and special offers, if you have opted-in to receive them.
    </li>
    <li>
      (d) To protect our rights and interests, such as by enforcing our terms of service, complying with legal obligations, and preventing fraud or abuse.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3. How We Share Your Information</h3>

  <div>
    We may share your personal information with third parties in the following circumstances:
  </div>

  <ul>
    <li>
      (a) Service Providers: We may share your information with third-party service providers that help us operate our business and provide our services, such as payment processors, email service providers, and customer support providers.
    </li>
    <li>
      (b) Legal Obligations: We may disclose your information when required by law, such as in response to a subpoena, court order, or government request.
    </li>
    <li>
      (c) Business Transfers: In the event of a merger, acquisition, or sale of our assets, we may transfer your information to the new owner.
    </li>
    <li>
      (d) Aggregate Information: We may share aggregated, non-personally identifiable information with third parties for research, marketing, or other purposes.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>4. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h3>

  <div class="mb-3">
    We use an essential session cookie to provide secure sign-in, forms, and account features. Google reCAPTCHA may also use browser technologies to protect public forms from spam and abuse. These technologies are necessary for the services you request.
  </div>

  <div class="mb-3">
    Google Analytics is optional and does not load unless you select <strong>Accept all cookies</strong> in our cookie banner. You can instead choose <strong>Use essential cookies only</strong>, or change your choice at any time using <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the footer. See our <%= link_to "Cookie Policy", cookie_policy_path %> for details.
  </div>

  <h3>5. Your Rights and Choices</h3>

  <div>
    You have the following rights and choices regarding your personal information:
  </div>

  <ul>
    <li>
      (a) Access and Update: You can access and update your personal information by logging into your user profile or contacting us at <a href="mailto:admin@arogyam.life">admin@arogyam.life</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      (b) Opt-Out: You can opt-out of receiving marketing communications by following the unsubscribe instructions in the emails we send or by contacting us at <a href="mailto:admin@arogyam.life">admin@arogyam.life</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      (c) Delete: You can request that we delete your personal information by contacting us at <a href="mailto:admin@arogyam.life">admin@arogyam.life</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>6. Security</h3>

  <div class="mb-3">
    We take reasonable precautions to protect your personal information from unauthorized access, use, or disclosure. However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee the absolute security of your information.
  </div>

  <h3>7. Changes to This Policy</h3>

  <div class="mb-3">
    We may update this Policy from time to time. If we make significant changes, we will notify you by email or by posting a prominent notice on our website. Where consent is required for a new purpose, we will request it separately.
  </div>

  <h3>8. Contact Us</h3>

  <div class="mb-3">
    If you have any questions or concerns about this Policy or our privacy practices, please contact us at:
  </div>

